  ('326721591894519794', 'Private Popsicle', 1982, 'Comedy, Romance', 'Boaz Davidson, Adam Greenberg, Shaul Dishy', 'Boaz Davidson', 'Yftach Katzur, Zachi Noy, Jonathan Sagall, Sonja Martin, Menashe Warshavsky, Bea Fiedler, Dietmar Siegert, Dvora Kedar', null, 'The Lemon Popsicle boys - Bobby, Benji, and Huey - have been drafted into the army, but they''re not quite ready to give up the freedom they''ve enjoyed for so long and submit to army discipline. They spend most of their time chasing women, trying to get out of doing any work and avoiding their no-nonsense sergeant.', 'The Lemon Popsicle boys - Bobby, Benji, and Huey - have been drafted into the army, but they''re not quite ready to give up the freedom they''ve enjoyed for so long and submit to army discipline. They spend most of their time chasing women, trying to get out of doing any work and avoiding their no-nonsense sergeant.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/rwyeRg7nqKhKKQBnSDPTE16bdbW.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:10583'),
  ('449511971969114306', 'Private Property', 1960, 'Thriller', 'Leslie Stevens, Ted D. McCord, Louis Brandt', 'Leslie Stevens', 'Warren Oates, Corey Allen, Kate Manx, Jerome Cowan, Robert Wark, Jules Maitland', null, 'A hoodlum plots to seduce a lonely housewife and turn her over to his virginal friend.', 'A hoodlum plots to seduce a lonely housewife and turn her over to his virginal friend.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/vfi9i5PTztkOgDgOcoSDI0jzDeh.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:251421'),
  ('622319967297753150', 'Private Property', 2006, 'Drama', 'Joachim Lafosse, Hichame Alaouié', 'François Pirot, Joachim Lafosse', 'Isabelle Huppert, Jérémie Renier, Yannick Renier, Patrick Descamps, Kris Cuppens, Raphaëlle Lubansu, Sabine Riche, Dirk Tuypens', null, 'Pascale leads a lonely life with her adult sons François and Thierry at a rural estate subsidized by her ex-husband''s alimony payments. When Pascale falls for neighbor Jan, she makes plans to move in with him. But Pascale''s twin sons -- loafers who treat her like a servant and refuse to accept the responsibilities of adulthood -- won''t let her go. The family remains locked in a stalemate until someone makes a startling move.', 'Pascale leads a lonely life with her adult sons François and Thierry at a rural estate subsidized by her ex-husband''s alimony payments. When Pascale falls for neighbor Jan, she makes plans to move in with him. But Pascale''s twin sons -- loafers who treat her like a servant and refuse to accept the responsibilities of adulthood -- won''t let her go. The family remains locked in a stalemate until someone makes a startling move.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/vmtN0M5KVcB38dedSa3p2L4rMEA.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:12156'),
